      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to explain without some numbers to look at. so i was using a synth to play a tritone-based cluster around 144Hz and 217Hz, but it wasn't quite right. then i drifted into this weird microtonal space where the ratio is something like 1.618... but slightly off, like a non-periodic sequence. when i held that, the \"pressure\" in the room became almost tactile. if we treat \"willpower\" as a cognitive resistance or a mental inertia, how would you model the frequency required to overcome that inertia? like, what kind of wave function would we need to describe a frequency that bypasses the conscious filter and hits the core intent?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
